--- !u!114 &1134663636
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1134663634}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 70c7cc5d303454b34ad9b8be327728bf, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Subnet.Hacking.HackableObstacle
  encounterTitle: WEEPING_COMMUTER.sys  //  'PETRIFIED'
  speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 56cd5503be0064943a9a0347db24263e, type: 2}
  introLines:
  - ...
  - Don't look at me. I'm not crying. Statues don't cry. Statues are fine.
  - '* She''s carved out of the same stone as the others. But the pixels running
    down her face are still warm.'
  - '* My handheld finds a memory inside her. Shattered into pieces.'
  waves:
  - pattern: 5
    duration: 9
    intensity: 1
  - pattern: 3
    duration: 9
    intensity: 1
  - pattern: 4
    duration: 10
    intensity: 1
  puzzles:
  - prompt: 'A broken memory: ''...the smell of ____ on hot asphalt.'' Reassemble
      it.'
    options:
    - '[EXHAUST FUMES]'
    - '[SUMMER RAIN]'
    - '[BURNT COFFEE]'
    correctIndex: 1
    correctLine: The stone around her shoulders softens. 'Summer rain... We used
      to run through it. On purpose.'
    wrongLine: The fragment doesn't fit. The stone gets a little colder.
  - prompt: 'Another piece: ''...my sister laughing at ____.'''
    options:
    - '[MY PRESENTATION]'
    - '[THE EVENING NEWS]'
    - '[A DOG CHASING ITS OWN TAIL]'
    correctIndex: 2
    correctLine: A crack runs down the stone. Inside, someone laughs, small and surprised.
    wrongLine: '''No... she never laughed at that.'' The pixels fall faster.'
  - prompt: 'The last piece. She whispers: ''I''m not broken. I''m ____.'''
    options:
    - '[OBSOLETE]'
    - '[TIRED, AND THAT''S ALLOWED]'
    - '[FINE. I''M FINE.]'
    correctIndex: 1
    correctLine: '''...Tired. And that''s allowed.'' She says it twice, like she''s
      trying it on.'
    wrongLine: '''Fine.'' The word lands like another layer of concrete.'
  resolutionLines:
  - The stone cracks open. Underneath, a person. Breathing.
  - Thank you. I forgot I was allowed to cry and keep going at the same time.
  - '* Warm pixels drift up into the gray sky. The corridor ahead is clear.'
  portraitTarget: {fileID: 1033093982}
  portraitDistance: 2.2
  betweenRoundLines:
  - ...We ran through the rain on purpose. Mom was so mad. We were so happy.
  - She laughed so hard she snorted. I'd forgotten that sound.
  tauntLines:
  - Don't look at me.
  - I'm fine. I'm FINE.
  - Statues don't cry.
  - Everyone else is coping. Why can't I?
  - Go away... no, wait.
  - It's just concrete in my eyes.
  musicOverride: {fileID: 0}
  requiredFlag: park_puzzle_solved
  lockedLines:
  - '* Sealed behind concrete.'
  flagOnResolved: hack2_done
  hideOnResolved:
  - {fileID: 1689903893}
  showOnResolved:
  - {fileID: 597806655}
  - {fileID: 904751430}
  dissolveColor: {r: 1, g: 0.75, b: 0.45, a: 1}
  promptAnchor: {fileID: 0}
  onResolved:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
